00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Obviously, John Mulaney,
that was a given...

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:05.505
But "The Sack Lunch Bunch,
where did you come up with that?

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:06.306 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-"The Sack Lunch Bunch"?

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:09.175 size:84% position:42%
I wanted, like, a name
of, like, a groovy old,

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.610 line:92%
like, name, like, in the '70s.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, there would be shows
that were like, you know,

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:13.680 line:92%
The Scrapyard Gang and stuff

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I wanted to call it
"The Latchkey Kids" 'cause -

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you remember that term?
-Yes.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was, like,
a latchkey kid, I guess,

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:23.490
'cause my parents had jobs
so we'd come home, you know?

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we'd watch TV,
and we'd enjoy it.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
And on the news,
they'd be like,

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:31.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Latchkey kids.
It's a terrible thing."

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:33.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we'd be like,
"No, it's not."

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:35.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, then,
Sack Lunch Bunch, you know -

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:38.204 size:81% position:41%
Two words of it rhyme.
-Yeah, there you go.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.672 line:92%
-Not a lot of science to it.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.876
-You -- There are so many
wonderful songs in this.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Wonderful composer,
Eli Bolin.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:46.046 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Eli Bolin. Yeah.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Who we worked with
on "Documentary Now!"

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Documentary Now!"
He's fantastic.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've written songs
together before.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You wrote an
Emmy Award-winning song.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.154
-We won an Emmy. We wrote a song
with Justin Timberlake.

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:57.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we won an Emmy.
-Yeah. Now, question.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:00:59.392 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We want to -- Okay.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:04.864
So, this song was a monologu
song for Justin Timberlake

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.233 line:92%
On the ballot of the Emmys

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
it said
"Justin Timberlake Song."

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Then below it was the muc

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:14.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
more popular "Mother Lover
by The Lonely Island...

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:17.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Justin Timberlake
and Andy Samberg.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.278 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:21.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But ours was called
"The Justin Timberlake Song.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we won.
-Yeah.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:26.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've always wondered,
do you think people though

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:29.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
that that was
The Lonely Island song?

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:29.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:30.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think it's, like,
those weird --

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, when they have, like
